{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall put on his linen tunic</b> — this is the כֻּתֹּנֶת. And what does the term \"מִדּוֹ\" teach? That it must be to his measure. <b>Upon his flesh</b> — that nothing shall intervene between them; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 6:3). Now, the removal of the ashes requires the priestly vestments, and there is no service performed in only two of them, but Scripture mentioned these two because of a matter that is newly taught here: to say that the כֻּתֹּנֶת must be to his measure. The point is to say that if they were shortened, too short and not reaching his feet, and he performed his service in them, the service is invalid. And it teaches that there shall be nothing between him and the מִכְנָסַיִם and his flesh at all — and the same holds for all priestly vestments. For once Scripture mentioned that it requires vestments, we learn that it requires four for the ordinary priest and eight for the High Priest. And so it is explicit in tractate Yoma in the second chapter (23a) and in Torat Kohanim (Sifra, Tzav 1:1): What does \"יִלְבָּשׁ\" teach? To include the מִצְנֶפֶת and the אַבְנֵט. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Leviticus 6:3) translated \"מִדּוֹ\" as \"לְבוּשִׁין\" — and it appears that in his usage \"מִדּוֹ\" is a noun that includes all his garments, as though it said: and the priest shall put on linen garments. Similarly, \"his מַדָּיו were torn\" (1 Samuel 4:12), \"it descends upon the mouth of his מִדּוֹתָיו\" (Psalms 133:2) — upon the mouth of his garments; \"girt with his מִדּוֹ, his garment\" (2 Samuel 20:8). And this would accord with the opinion that says: the אַבְנֵט of an ordinary priest is not the same as the אַבְנֵט of the High Priest (Yoma 12)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The parenthetical reference '(כג)' appears to point to Yoma 23a-b, where the relevant halakhic discussion is found; the exact page reference may reflect a variant numbering. Similarly '(צו ב א)' refers to Sifra on the parashah of Tzav, chapter 1, section 1."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:21.035245174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}